@startuml
title Employee & Task Management System — Use Cases
left to right direction
actor "Authenticated user" as User
actor ADMIN as Admin
actor MANAGER as Manager
actor EMPLOYEE as Employee
User <|-- Admin
User <|-- Manager
User <|-- Employee
rectangle "Employee & Task Management System" {
  usecase "Sign in / sign out" as Login
  usecase "View scoped dashboard" as Dashboard
  usecase "View task list and details" as View
  usecase "Create / view / edit / delete users" as Users
  usecase "Create / edit / delete any task" as AllTasks
  usecase "Download all-task PDF report" as AllPdf
  usecase "Assign tasks to own team" as Assign
  usecase "Edit own-assigned tasks" as Edit
  usecase "Download current-team PDF report" as TeamPdf
  usecase "View own assigned tasks" as Own
  usecase "Start own task\nPENDING to IN_PROGRESS" as Start
  usecase "Complete own task\nIN_PROGRESS to DONE" as Done
}
User -- Login
User -- Dashboard
User -- View
Admin -- Users
Admin -- AllTasks
Admin -- AllPdf
Manager -- Assign
Manager -- Edit
Manager -- TeamPdf
Employee -- Own
Employee -- Start
Employee -- Done
note bottom of TeamPdf
Includes tasks assigned by ADMIN to current team employees.
Task list/dashboard show only the manager's original assignments.
Report access does not grant editing permission.
end note
note bottom of Users
Delete sets active=false and preserves task history.
end note
note bottom of Login
Sign-out clears browser session; no token revocation endpoint.
Protected actions require valid JWT and current active DB account.
end note
@enduml
